# Dinah Boswell: why her fobs were not sent for update

Date: 2026-09-04. Prod read-only pull against tenant `south-melb-lsc`, deployed code v1.15.0 (commit `1ded11a`, live since 2 Sep 17:44 AEST). No production writes were made.

## Answer

Dinah's fobs were never sent to the programmer because her renewal attestation was never completed. The membership admin renewed her on 8 Aug, the attestation email was delivered to her address, she did not respond within the 7-day token window, and the nightly job marked the attestation expired on 16 Aug. Only a completed attestation (or an admin force renew) touches credentials, so her two fobs kept their 31 Aug expiry, expired at midnight on 1 Sep, and were never flagged `programming_required`. The daily programmer summary selects exclusively on that flag, so there was nothing to send.

The misleading part is that her member page says she is renewed. The renew action writes `current_season = 2026/2027` and `status = active` onto the membership at the moment the admin clicks Renew, before the member has attested. So the membership reads as renewed for the new season while the credentials underneath were never staged for update.

