## Corrective action for Dinah

Recommended: open her member page and use **Resend attestation** (fresh 7-day token). When she confirms her fobs, both are flagged with `pending_expires_at = 1 Sep 2027` and appear in the next 2am summary under "Credentials Awaiting Reprogramming"; the programmer then uses confirm programming, which promotes the expiry and reactivates the fobs.

If she is unreachable and the club wants her access restored anyway: **Force Renew** will NOT work as she stands, because it only rewrites expiry on ACTIVE credentials and hers are EXPIRED (`force-renew/route.ts:91-100`). It would also skip the programmer entirely even on active fobs (see defect 2). The only bypass today is a direct data fix: set `programming_required = true`, `programming_reason`, `pending_expires_at = 2027-08-31 14:00 UTC` on both credentials, then the summary and confirm-programming flow take over.

## Defects and process gaps surfaced

1. **Renewed-before-attested membership state.** `members/[id]/renew/route.ts:64-71` sets season and active on the membership at click time. Admins read that as renewed. Either defer the season write to attestation completion, or show attestation status prominently beside the season on the member list and page.
2. **Force Renew bypasses the programmer.** `force-renew/route.ts:84-124` writes `expires_at` directly with no `programming_required`, no `pending_expires_at`, and only for ACTIVE credentials. Every admin-bypass renewal silently skips reprogramming, and it does nothing at all after 1 Sep once fobs have expired. Should stage the expiry and flag exactly as the attestation route does, and include EXPIRED credentials.
3. **Expired attestations are invisible.** Cron 1b marks them expired and nothing follows: no reminder to the member, no line in the daily summary, no member-list filter. At least 5 attestations for 2026/2027 are expired and 7 pending as of this pull (attestation list in Appendix B), so Dinah is not alone. A "Renewals awaiting attestation" section in the summary for the renew permission, plus an automatic resend at token expiry, would close this.

